  "blockingGaps": [
    "Terraform owns seven locally archived controller releases with checked SHA-256 locks and an optional GitOps root, but the default private EKS API is unreachable from an external Terraform runner; live CRD/webhook/application health remain unproven",
    "The data Application covers Kafka, RabbitMQ and Redis manifests; RDS bootstrap and eleven PostgreSQL owner migration Jobs render offline. PgBouncer, Kafka topics, Connect, OpenSearch and Cassandra have conditional digest-pinned Argo children. Cassandra TLS/auth/schema/role bootstrap and OpenSearch TLS/scoped users have local proof, but their Secret values, image promotion, Argo ordering, EKS behavior, rotation, storage recovery and teardown lack live proof. MQTT now has a private digest-pinned Argo child and worker TLS/CA/NetworkPolicy wiring; broker and device credential equality, certificate/ACL verification, external device access, connector/schema registration and live RDS/RLS proof remain missing",
    "CI digest assembly and GHCR-to-ECR promotion have only offline proof; ECR publication, node pull and deployment values have no live proof",
    "Secret containers and a guarded one-shot sync exist without operator source values, automatic rotation or live proof; service and in-cluster data NetworkPolicy links render and VPC CNI policy support is configured, but enforcement and external database, identity and provider egress require live proof/design",
    "New runtime images and Helm profiles need built/published digests, secrets, data egress and live startup proof; search-indexer quarantine PVC needs live binding proof",
    "Stage 11 observability has digest-pinned OTel/Prometheus/Grafana/Tempo/Loki ownership plus offline OTLP/HTTP and scrape wiring, but image execution, dashboards, alert routing, backend access and real end-to-end telemetry are unvalidated",
    "No AWS web/iPhone acceptance or teardown proof"
  ]
}
